# Accepted Trivy misconfiguration findings. Each needs a reason; review when Trivy is bumped.

# False positive: flags the ConfigMap key "PORT" (value 8080) as sensitive content.
# The ConfigMap holds only APP_ENV, LOG_FORMAT, PORT, RUST_LOG. Secrets go in SealedSecrets.
KSV-01010

# ghcr.io is this project's registry; Trivy's built-in trusted list does not include it.
# Images are additionally pinned by sha256 digest (enforced by scripts/policy_check.py).
KSV-0125

# Deliberate: CPU requests are set, CPU limits are not, to avoid CFS throttling of a
# latency-sensitive HTTP service. Memory limits ARE set (enforced by policy_check.py).
KSV-0011

# Sealed Secrets controller (platform/sealed-secrets), inherent to its job:
# KSV-0041: ClusterRole `secrets-unsealer` manages Secrets. It is NOT bound cluster-wide
#   (upstream ClusterRoleBinding deleted); it is bound per namespace by
#   components/sealed-secrets-access, and policy_check.py allows only that binding.
KSV-0041
# KSV-0113: Role `sealed-secrets-key-admin` manages Secrets in the controller's own
#   namespace: that is where the sealing keys are stored.
KSV-0113
